From fd567b4cb158f7e3a5d20f9d6f351b9ba6660d3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:12:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): one early notice for a wake probe that cannot
 pass under a far backstop [daveey]

A card parked on a probe that can never become true (t_eeeeee0000000016 run 6: a probe passing only when a
restarting service's PID is gone) sat `scheduled` for 17.7 h with no notice; the existing wake_check_stale
wake fires only at 48 h.

Extends the wake-episode path (kanban_wake_episode.not_yet) with detection only: after >= 3 clean exit-1
checks spanning more than kanban.wake_check_notice_hours (default 6) within the current park, while the
park's wake_at backstop is more than 24 h away, append ONE passive `wake_probe_unproven_notice` naming the
probe and its last output (delivered to the origin chat by the gateway and TUI notifiers; never wakes it).
One per park episode (a re-park opens a new one); clock_only parks never notify. Probe semantics, backstops,
admission and the 48 h wake are unchanged.

RED/GREEN: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_wake_unproven.py (2 positive tests failed before the hook).
